  patterns, and git matches those at ANY depth: logs at .gitignore:26, bin at
  :7, target at :6, activemq-data at :25 and partition-descriptor at :24 are
  all ignored wherever they appear, as is builds/ at :40.  Re-verified at this
  directory's exact depth with a .log file inside each candidate rather than
  taken on trust: all six resolve to IGNORED, and this file's own path resolves
  to no match and is committable.  The ignored token is always the DIRECTORY
  name and never the .log file extension, so a .log placed inside a directory
  named logs would be silently uncommitted while every local check still
  passed.  This file therefore sits directly in startup/ and no subdirectory
  was created beneath it.
