- Governing rule on evidence, verbatim: "Validation asserts on produced
  artifacts and captured output, never on process exit status alone. This is
  mandatory rather than stylistic because Gruntfile.js sets
  grunt.option('force', true), which masks task failures and lets a broken
  build exit zero."  Applied here without softening: successful scanning is
  asserted on the CAPTURED REGION, never on the deployment's exit status and
  never on a healthy readiness probe.  The asymmetry is real in this
  application, because the startup-time asset build runs through that same
  forced-execution pipeline, so a deployment can reach ready state with a
  broken build behind it.  A container that started is not the same thing as a
  scan that completed, and only the region can tell the two apart.  This region
  is empty, so nothing is asserted from it - which is the rule applied, not the
  rule evaded.
- Governing rule on ambiguity, verbatim: "The application's observed behavior
  at the base commit on JDK 8 is the tie-breaker for any ambiguity, and each
