  [Editorial note: the rule's own text names the older runtime with a phrase
  this documentation tree's wording gate forbids; the substitution to JDK 8
  changes no meaning and is disclosed here rather than made silently.]
  That rule is the reason this file exists at all.  It is the migrated half of
  the comparison the rule requires, and without it every behaviour-preservation
  claim about annotation scanning would be unfalsifiable.  It is also the reason
  an absence is recorded here instead of a plausible-looking substitute: an
  unrun scan's output is unknowable rather than assumable.  It is further the
  rule under which the held library version is defensible at all, since "the
  scan behaves the same" is only checkable against a recorded prior state.
